# ThreadSanitizer suppressions for PathFinder.
#
# Usage:
#   TSAN_OPTIONS="suppressions=$(pwd)/sanitizers/tsan.supp" make launch-car HEADLESS=true
#
# Each entry below matches a race report that originates entirely inside a
# third-party library, NOT in PathFinder source. They are kept as suppressions
# rather than fixes because they are upstream bugs we cannot touch from this
# repo. Re-evaluate after any ROS 2 / FastDDS / DDS-vendor upgrade — if these
# fire on patterns that LOOK like the existing ones but with new symbols,
# investigate before adding a new entry: a real race in our code might be
# masquerading as familiar noise.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# FastDDS shared-memory transport: receive-payload-pool race.
#
# When the SHM transport delivers a message to a subscribing rclcpp::Node,
# FastDDS's eprosima::fastrtps::rtps::TopicPayloadPool::get_payload is called
# on one DDS thread while eprosima::fastcdr::Cdr::deserialize_array runs on
# another. TSan sees concurrent access on the payload buffer. This is internal
# FastDDS state — our nodes only see fully-deserialized messages by the time
# the subscription callback fires. Reported many times upstream against
# eprosima/Fast-DDS; fixed in newer FastDDS releases but ROS 2 Jazzy still
# ships a version where this trips.
race:eprosima::fastrtps::rtps::TopicPayloadPool::get_payload
race:eprosima::fastcdr::Cdr::deserialize_array
